Joshua Nazaire - Project B: System Calls

WHAT I DID
- printString: prints a null-terminated string using BIOS interrupt 0x10
- readString: reads a line from the keyboard with interrupt 0x16, echoes
  characters, handles Backspace, and ends the line with 0xa and 0x0
- readSector: reads a disk sector into a buffer using interrupt 0x13
- Created interrupt 0x21 (makeInterrupt21 and handleInterrupt21)
- handleInterrupt21 provides: AX=0 print string, AX=1 read string,
  AX=2 read sector, AX>=3 prints an error message

HOW TO VERIFY
1. Run ./compileOS.sh to build diskc.img (needs nasm, bcc, as86, ld86)
2. Open Emumaker86 (simulator.jar), choose diskc.img for Hard Drive C,
   enter 63 cylinders, 255 heads, 1000 sectors, and click Boot Disk C
3. The program prints "Enter a line:". Type a line and press Enter.
4. Your line is echoed back, then the contents of sector 30 print:
   "If this message prints out, then your readSector function is
   working correctly!"
All of these go through interrupt 0x21.

FILES
kernel.c, kernel.asm, bootload.asm, compileOS.sh, message.txt, diskc.img
